Solve the following system using the Chinese Remainder Theorem:
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 1 \pmod{5}\\
x \equiv 2 \pmod{7}\\
x \equiv 3 \pmod{9}
\end{cases}
\]

Determine whether the following system has a solution. If yes, find it:
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 3 \pmod{6}\\
x \equiv 5 \pmod{9}
\end{cases}
\]
